\begin_layout Section
Interoperability
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A major barrier in cross-language workflows is the incompatibility of data serialization formats (R’s RDS vs.
 Python’s Pickle).
 BiocPy addresses this challenge through two primary approaches:
 direct binary ingestion via rds2py and language-agnostic interchange via ArtifactDB.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Direct Ingestion with rds2py
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
BiocPy provides rds2py,
 a package that can read R’s binary serialization format (RDS).
 This allows Python environments to ingest complex S4 objects directly from disk without requiring an installed R runtime.
 rds2py implements memory-efficient loading strategies rather than performing deep copies where ever possible.
 This is essential when loading large Bioconductor objects for downstream analyses in Python.
\end_layout

