\begin_layout Subsection
Advanced Genomic Integration
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
BiocPy’s GenomicRanges serves as a bridge between biological semantics and the general-purpose Python data stack.
 In this scenario,
 we analyze ChIP-seq peaks by filtering for promoter region and visualizing the results using seaborn,
 a popular Python plotting library.
 This demonstrates how BiocPy handles the biological complexity (strand-aware resizing) while delegating visualization to standard Python tools.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
